From: scriptc tests/perf/zapo-rest
Subject: serialise history-sync chunk processing

zapo-js v1.6.2, commit 250f9af5229a545eec28ddbd3e8774a397cdb0bb.

Why, and what it is worth, is in tests/perf/zapo-rest/README.md under
"The peak of a history sync". In one line: nothing serialises
runHistorySyncNotification, so a sync's peak is the whole sync and not one
chunk, and the fix is a five-line promise gate that costs no throughput.

The one risk this carries: the hist_sync receipt for chunk N is now sent after
chunks 1..N-1 have been written, so a phone whose resend timer is shorter than
the serialised backlog would resend. Measured backlog for a 19,200-message sync
is 4.6 s end to end.

---
--- a/src/client/WaClient.ts
+++ b/src/client/WaClient.ts
@@ -70,12 +70,24 @@
     private readonly mediaTransfer!: WaMediaTransferClient
     private readonly writeBehind!: WriteBehindPersistence
     private connectPromise: Promise<void> | null = null
     private acceptingIncomingEvents = true
     private activeIncomingHandlers = 0
     private readonly incomingHandlersDrainedWaiters: Array<() => void> = []
+    /* One history-sync chunk at a time. The stanza pipeline dispatches incoming
+     * messages fire-and-forget (`void runtime.handleIncomingMessageEvent(event)`
+     * in WaClientFactory), so without this gate every chunk WhatsApp pushes
+     * decodes and persists concurrently and the process's peak is the whole
+     * sync rather than one chunk. Measured on the compiled REST service at
+     * 19,200 messages in 8 chunks: 211 -> 79 MiB peak working set, 582 -> 144
+     * MiB peak private commit, and the sync finishes in 4.6 s instead of 11.9 s
+     * because eight concurrent decodes thrash where one does not. It also makes
+     * the `history_sync_chunk` events arrive in chunk order, which the
+     * concurrent path does not: 2 of 7 unserialised runs ended with a final
+     * reported `progress` of 25 after having already reported 100. */
+    private historySyncChunkGate: Promise<void> = Promise.resolve()
     private disposePlugins: (() => Promise<void>) | null = null
     private readonly pluginInstallInput!: WaClientPluginInstallInput
 
